        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your patient, a 66-year-old male, admitted on 01/10/2022 with an acute exacerbation of known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD). On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Spirometry supported severe obstructive ventilatory impairment. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 02/10/2022 with oral steroids, inhaler therapy, and outpatient pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation action plan was provided. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Kind regards, Dr. [Treating Physician].</div>"
            },
